WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.600
This girl is Kouyama Mitsuki. 12 years old.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.260
Her debut single as Full Moon, 
"Myself", is now on sale.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.920
She thought the debut would cause an uproar in her class...

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.500
...but the rumors going around were different.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.670
She was really disappointed.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.100
But, with my loud voice, I managed to advertise for her.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.960
Now that she's befriended her classmates,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.910
she's really happy now.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.070
Well, then...

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.870
...I wonder what's going to happen today.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.500
Huh?

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.820
Do you understand?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.760
Yes.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.160
Mitsukinchin, who'll come? {LOL @ her nickname}

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.370
My grandmother originally planned to come.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.110
But she caught a cold this morning.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.730
So, no one will come.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:22.940
Ah, I see.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.270
Who is that..? {Fangirl Alert!!!}

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.300
Could he be... {Fangirl Alert!!!}

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.780
Don't tell me... {Fangirl Alert!!!}

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.950
...<i>The Prince?</i> {Capitalized since that's how Route L fans refer to Wakaouji as}

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:32.580
Eh?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.450
See? Don't you remember?

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.080
From Route L... {Total mistranslation originally, since when did I become qualified to be a Translation Checker, lol}

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.040
The Prince?

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.000
Who's that?

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.630
He's so cool!

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.420
Wakaouji-sensei...

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:48.630
Dr. Wakaouji, he really stands out in a place like this... definitely.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.050
He reeks of medicine.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.160
Mitsuki-chan.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.880
Sensei, why are you here?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.440
Well, your grandmother is ill today,{}

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.080
and I heard that you had a Parents Day...{}

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.830
...so I came here instead.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.030
Thanks.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:21.880
Who's he?

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.150
Your dad? {Such is the life of a finish editor}

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.000
You never told me that your dad was so cool.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.430
No, he's not.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.300
He's not?

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.010
Well, Wakaouji-sensei is a friend of my dad.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.890
I see, so that's how it is.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:38.150
Am I troubling you by posing as your father?

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.230
Not at all! {Edited "That's not true" since she says "that's not the case... afterward}

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.000
That's not the case...

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.280
I admit that you really stand out.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:45.900
Eh?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.320
Oh my!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.420
Wakaouji-sensei, I listened to your story.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.250
It was really interesting.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.930
Not really.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.360
It's just my past.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.220
I felt very proud today.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:11.800
Attention everyone! {I should extract the color styling from the later episodes for the DJ since she's a recurring character, as well as Mitsuki's friends from school}

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.680
Next up is this month's latest rising star.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.390
With her big hit, Full Moon is next with "Myself".

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.080
She said it's a big hit!

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.070
Just like I told you, right?

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.280
Ahhh!{}

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.030
Shhh!!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.990
Yes, this is Wakaouji. {Cursed phone}

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.700
Hey, what's that all about?

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.230
Right while her song was playing...

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:53.260
...he just <i>had</i>  to pick up the phone. {This is all past tense, since he already picked up the phone}

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.430
Yes, right.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.510
Tomorrow we meet at the Taujo Hotel, right?

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.200
Here, show him the CD.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.200
Yes, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.230
So if you'd excuse me...{}

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:07.710
Sensei.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:08.130
Hmm?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:09.940
Want to hear some music?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:10.900
Here, this one!

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.300
Ah, sorry.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.400
This car is not equipped with a CD player.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.070
Well, how about if I give it to you... so you can play it at home?

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.080
See, she's really pretty, right?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.170
I'm sorry.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:29.590
Hmm?

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:35.200
The thing is... I never really 
listen to this kind of music. {Never alone seemed a tad too strong}

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.050
I'm already an old guy.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.870
What are you talking about?

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.060
Just listen to it.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.890
I think it's a very good song. {I couldn't agree more}

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:43.480
Really?

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.480
You like listening to music.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:48.730
Yes.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.960
Maybe, if I become a singer...

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:55.030
...I think this is the kind of song 
that I'd want to sing.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:59.450
That's why I want to know what you think of this song, Wakaouji-sensei.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:00.480
Please listen to it.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.220
I see.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.000
You want to become a singer.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.330
That's right.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.480
You told me countless times.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:07.290
Right.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:13.640
Ah, by the way, about the meeting today...

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.970
...that was a first for me, 
so I was very nervous.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:22.310
Hmph.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.520
Eh... um...

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.060
Uh... um...

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.840
Mitsuki-chan, what is it?

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.480
It's nothing.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.130
Why are you like that?

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.150
Stupid.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.430
For showing up at school today...

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.010
...I thank you for that.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:40.920
Mitsuki-chan!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.830
Sorry, did I say anything bad?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.330
No, you didn't.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:48.790
Really?

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.400
W-Well...

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.260
You should tell me if 
it was something I said.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.920
Nothing at all.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.220
Is that... so?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.440
That's right.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:00.600
With a cold guy like him, 
there's no use telling him.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.720
Sensei, you're cool... and you're smart as well.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:05.670
You're perfect.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.420
There's nothing to complain about.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:08.480
Mitsuki-chan.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:10.730
Ah?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:12.980
Ah...

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.230
I really am an old guy... I can't even understand a girl's feelings!

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:19.320
Ahhhhh!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.370
Grandma...

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.620
I've brought you some tea.{edited}

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.420
Ah, thank you.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.670
You must be hungry, Grand...{}

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:43.980
Mitsuki-san.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:45.310
Y-Yes?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.100
It's irritating.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:48.730
Could you turn it down, please?

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:49.810
S-Sure.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.940
My heart's beating so fast.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.040
Tanaka-san?

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.370
Mitsuki-chan?

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.620
Your earphones are not plugged it. {Oops}

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.420
I could hear it throughout the house.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.500
Oh, darn.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:16.800
My fault, my fault.{}

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.640
Hey, hey, we have a job today.

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:25.140
Yes.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.140
Yay, we're going out, we're going out!

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.870
Eh, you're going to see the doctor?

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.690
No, I can't.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.990
What, I have to stay?!

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.670
Meroko, you're annoying.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:47.960
Are you serious?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.210
It's really boring here!

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.050
Mitsuki-chan is not the social type...

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:00.260
A mature love is usually the key. {Shouldn't you be focusing on your duties as a Doctor, instead of reading magazines}

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.010
What... what?

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:05.970
Girls look for a father figure.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.030
That's so moving.

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:15.610
Huh, that can't be... like that...

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.960
No, Mitsuki-chan is not like that. {I don't want to know}

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.030
For the love of knowledge, I'll keep a copy.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.700
Well, this is for my love of knowledge...

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.300
Man, this is so boring!

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.420
I can't take it anymore!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.130
Thank you very much.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.120
Wasn't that a good session?

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.360
Especially that tune.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.020
Yes.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.440
Here, what do you think this is? {who is making the money here, they never talk about monies $$}

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.390
What is it?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:01.900
The song's such a big hit, 
stores keep asking for more!

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.080
I see.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:05.860
It's really selling.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.580
What is it? You're not happy?

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.450
No, that's not the case.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.600
You don't seem very energetic.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:15.010
No, I'm fine.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:16.570
I see.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:17.790
It's really selling.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.920
Well, we'll split here.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.380
Take care on your way back.{}

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:27.190
Okay.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.430
Thank you very much.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.310
You're worried about something.

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:39.480
Why do you say that?

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:40.400
"Why?"

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.480
It's written all over your face.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.970
The doctor and your grandmother...{}

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:48.000
<i>They won't listen to my song.</i>

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.730
<i>So now I'm sad.</i>

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.620
Really?

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.130
Stupid, I don't mean literally.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:53.600
Eh?

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:55.910
It's a big hit, isn't it?

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.330
But, I...

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.380
I kept thinking about it, 
but I wanted to be happy.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.820
My dad composed a song...

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.520
...I passed the audition with it...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.680
...and now I'm a singer.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:15.060
However, despite that fact,
Wakaouji-sensei won't listen to it.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.140
Somehow...

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.980
...I feel like even Dad wouldn't 
recognize my song. {removed my, or it should be "my dad - lowercase"}

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.180
I don't think so.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:23.550
Eh?

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.220
You have a good voice.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.580
You put your best effort into that song.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.800
Even so...

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.780
That proves it.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.760
W-What is it?

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.720
Takuto, you don't know anything about music. {O RLY}

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:40.420
That's why you said those things so easily.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.060
Ah.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.050
S-Sorry, I went over the line.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.340
Um...

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:52.680
I'll go first.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:53.830
I...

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:56.100
I...

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.520
I was a musician in the past.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:00.190
Eh?

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.600
Papa, over here!

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.420
Wait a second.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:25.880
Takuto.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.050
What did you just say?

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.510
I was a musician in the past.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.460
In the past?

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:36.470
When I was a human, I used to sing too.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:40.080
Eh, Takuto used to be a human?! {Mitsuki is so adorable when she says that}

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.440
Hmph, I wasn't born as a Shinigami from the start.

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.910
Eh, no way!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.110
I never knew.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.660
Well, how about Meroko?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.300
Was Meroko a human, too?{}

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:50.580
I don't know her that well. {Meroko will kill you for saying that!}

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.400
But, I think so.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.820
So that's how it is...

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.370
Sorry... for saying that you didn't know anything about music.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.170
That's alright.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.200
Don't worry about it.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:03.370
Let's go.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.020
Eh?

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:05.750
Where to?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:07.750
Your song.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.420
You want him to listen, right?

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:13.430
Dr. Wakaouji is out for a meeting today.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:15.390
Yes, right.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.910
He has a meeting.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.390
Now that I think about it...

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.600
Alright, we're going to the Taujo Hotel!

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.520
Ah, w-wait!

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:27.730
Eh, was I wrong?

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:28.610
Yeah.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:34.360
He said something about a special favor and he sent someone else instead.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.560
I don't see him.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.200
We came here uninvited... won't we be bothering Sensei?

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.470
How could you say that?

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.260
We won't know until we try.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.340
But...

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:00.920
If he really doesn't like listening to music, what should we do?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:01.900
Aw, geez!

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.240
Don't hesitate now!

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.240
Let's go in! {I may edit that}

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:05.800
Have more confidence in yourself!

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.440
Right, right. {WB Meroko WB}

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:08.970
Meroko? {Yep! and with full spirit (form) too! :D}

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.280
What are you doing here?

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.470
That's because...!

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:13.160
You two always go out!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.740
Being by myself is so boring!

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.160
But, what about...

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.160
It's alright.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.850
Since your grandmother 
has a cold, she won't check.{}

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.430
Today, she'll be bedridden all day long. {what a mean thing to say, shame on you mero mero}

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:24.540
We won't get discovered.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.220
Ah, there it is!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.580
Who are you looking for?

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.970
Um, I'm looking for Wakaouji-sensei...

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.080
I'm really sorry.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.310
If you're not on the guest list, you're not allowed to go in.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:50.080
Tsk, and we've already gotten this far!

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.110
I was pretty sure he'd be here.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.130
I know!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:56.280
I'll make Dr. Wakaouji listen to the CD.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.530
But, but...

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.240
Meroko, not again...?! {9 episodes in, and a.f.k finally went with ?!"}

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.040
Anyways, we just want him to listen, right?

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.040
Meroko!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.170
Ah, where are you going?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.920
Takuto, what'll we do?

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.840
Heh, this should do it.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.670
Geez, that Meroko...

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.160
Where did she go?

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.800
Darn her.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.360
How could you say that to me?!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.240
No, I'm certain of it?!

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.320
Hey, what's going on here?

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.940
There's some weird music for the meeting upstairs.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.400
It's a wonderful song, nonetheless.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:38.680
Let's go see!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:39.200
Sure.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.170
Now's our chance! {Japan and teh engrish}

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:51.330
Well, this background music is pretty good. {It calms down even corporate cutthroats}

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.420
I don't see him.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:54.420
Ehhhh?

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.240
Hurry up! Just ask someone!

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:57.640
Okay.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:00.830
What was that all about?

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.240
I wonder if this music is 
part of their service? {What is with these eyecancerous colors for the subs in this episode}

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.240
Excuse me, I'm sorry... {LOL}

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:06.000
Where's Wakaouji-sensei?{BEST MOMENT EVER!}

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.740
Oh, Wakaouji-kun?

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.750
He's not attending the meeting today.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:10.310
Eh?

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.270
Where did he go?

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:13.880
How was it?

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.260
Today was perfect, right?

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:18.070
Hmm, if only that doctor was here.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:20.280
Eh, he's not here?

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:20.910
Oh crap... {Localized it, they had gulp for this line}

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:23.710
Did you get the place?

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:24.240
Yeah.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:26.500
Let's see...

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:41.970
This place is...

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.640
Is it a place you know?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:45.990
Yeah.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:49.350
I came here once before.

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:50.350
Really?

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:56.150
Ah.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.700
Wakaouji-sensei!

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:25.760
It's been ten years since you left. {intentionally changed from "died" to "left"}

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:30.210
Your daughter now is twelve years old.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:33.020
She's a strong girl.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.270
Just like Hazuki-san.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:43.580
If not for you two, I would've always run away.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.700
Every time I see Mitsuki-chan, she reminds me more and more of Hazuki-san. {I'll come up with an edit, that is the edit, hope it makes more sense}

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:51.120
It's almost like going back in time.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:55.480
This is too painful for me.{edited}

00:17:56.130 --> 00:18:00.130
Mitsuki-chan is now looking into the future.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.590
I can't let the wounds of the past haunt me.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:10.250
I hope you two can give me the strength to get through all of this.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.560
For a long time, I kept silent...

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.480
...about my music.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:41.630
I thought that I'd never have to deal with music ever again.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.170
But your daughter wants to become a singer.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.000
I guess she's just like her parents.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.560
As your daughter continues to grow...{still weird, but less weird than "...is taking shape..."}

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:55.060
I kept getting reminded of you.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:59.610
Both of you, together with me...

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.020
...please protect her.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.780
He's coming this way!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.270
Dad, Mom...

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.450
Mitsuki has debuted.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.790
Please cheer for me.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:05.590
I...

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.270
...will do my best.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:16.470
Is Wakaouji-sensei here?

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.310
Oh, Mitsuki-chan!

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.110
Sensei, can I...

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.120
Ah, sorry!

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:22.440
There's an emergency.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.680
I'll be right back.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:27.900
Geez, he's always busy.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:33.160
Is that...?

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.700
Sensei!

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.750
You bought it too!

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:41.370
Sorry...

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.480
...for making you wai...

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:43.670
Huh?

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:45.240
Mitsuki-chan?

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.110
She went home?

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:50.460
That can't be helped.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.730
<i>Thank you for stopping by on Parents Day!</i>

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:04.550
<i>It was a little bit awkward...</i>

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:07.040
<i>...but I was very happy!</i>

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:11.510
<i>From now on, you can pose as my dad, okay.</i>

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.450
From, Mitsuki.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:28.000
Sensei... I wonder if he's reading the card right now.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:09.510
What is it Meroko?

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:10.860
Grinning all by yourself...

00:23:11.150 --> 00:23:12.010
Because...!

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:13.720
Takuto, aren't you glad?

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:16.020
TV appearance! TV appearance!

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:18.850
Look to the right and left, there are so many celebrities!

00:23:18.850 --> 00:23:19.520
Darn it!

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:21.760
It's supposed to be her appearance, not ours!

00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:23.330
But, see... she's happy too.

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:26.540
Ah, you two!, When will it stop!

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.510
Is this gonna be okay?

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:30.700
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.570
The Law of Show Business!? {removed parentheses to keep consistency and kept interrobang same as the episode title}
